# Rust coding guidelines

- Use `./script/clippy` instead of `cargo clippy`
- Use `anyhow` for error handling in application code; prefer `?` over `unwrap()`
- Avoid `unwrap()` across FFI boundaries — a panic across JNI/C is undefined behaviour

---

# Skills

Detailed quick-reference documentation is in `.skills/`. Load the relevant file(s) before working on any of the topics below.

## GPUI framework — `.skills/gpui.md`

Context types (`App`, `Context<T>`, `Window`, `AsyncApp`), entities (`Entity<T>`, `WeakEntity<T>`), rendering (`Render`, `RenderOnce`), styling and layout, input events, actions, focus management, entity events and subscriptions, concurrency (`cx.spawn`, `cx.background_spawn`, `Task<R>`), global state, custom elements, notify, per-frame keyed state (`use_keyed_state`), app setup, error handling, recent API changes (never use `Model<T>`, `View<T>`, `WindowContext`, `ViewContext<T>`, `ModelContext<T>`), Rust 2024 borrow checker gotchas.

## gpui-component library — `.skills/gpui-component.md`

Setup and `Root` overlay layers, required trait imports, layout helpers (`h_flex`, `v_flex`), theming (`ActiveTheme`, `cx.theme()`), and all components: Button, Tag, Toggle, Switch, Checkbox, Input, Slider, Select, Form/Field, Tabs, List, Dialog, Notification (toast), Popover, Divider, Label, Progress, Spinner, Tooltip, Icon, Sidebar, Command Palette. Common patterns: entity creation, subscriptions, conditional rendering, `AnyElement`, Rust 2024 gotchas, collapsible sections, loading data from stores.

## gpui_transitions crate — `.skills/gpui_transitions.md`

Animated value transitions. Setup (including required `[patch.crates-io]` in workspace `Cargo.toml`), `Transition<T>`, `Lerp` trait, `BoolLerp<N>`, `WindowUseTransition` extension (`use_keyed_transition`, `use_transition`), evaluating, updating goals, easing functions, continuous mode, `use_keyed_state` (non-animated sibling).

## Android + Rust JNI — `.skills/android.md`

Calling Rust from Kotlin via a `cdylib` bridge crate. Architecture (no business logic in Kotlin), JNI naming convention, impl/wrapper split pattern, `cargo-ndk` build commands, `RustBridge` object, database path from Kotlin, data classes + `kotlinx.serialization`, repository pattern (`Dispatchers.IO`), ViewModel + `StateFlow<UiState>`, Gradle/KGP 2.x config gotchas, serde gotchas (`chrono::Duration`, `uuid`, `bitflags`).

## Android Compose Material 3 Expressive — `.skills/compose.md`

Dependencies (use `compose-bom-alpha` for Expressive), Activity setup, Navigation 3, Scaffold, Buttons with `shapes`, `SplitButtonLayout`, `ButtonGroup`, `FloatingActionButtonMenu` + `ToggleFloatingActionButton`, `HorizontalFloatingToolbar`, `FlexibleBottomAppBar`, `WideNavigationRail`, wavy/loading progress indicators, `TopAppBar`, `LazyColumn`, theming, accessibility, Gradle notes.

## Wear OS standalone app — `.skills/wear-os.md`

Standalone Wear OS app with Kotlin/Compose (no companion dependency required). Dependencies and `build.gradle.kts` (Wear Compose versioned independently — no BOM), `AppScaffold` + `ScreenScaffold`, `TransformingLazyColumn` (three required pieces: `transformedHeight`, `SurfaceTransformation`, `rememberTransformationSpec`), non-clickable `Card` (1.6+), scroll performance rules, architecture pattern (`Refreshing` state, optimistic mutations), phone ↔ watch communication via `MessageClient` (foreground + background listener wiring, `WearableListenerService`), deployment (`adb -t <transport-id>`), Tiles, Complications.

## Wear Compose Material 3 components — `.skills/wear-compose.md`

Screen structure, `TransformingLazyColumn` details, navigation (`SwipeDismissableNavHost`, Navigation3), buttons with shape morphing, `EdgeButton`, `ButtonGroup`, toggle controls, dialogs, pickers, progress indicators, cards, pagers, `SwipeToReveal`, sliders/steppers, ripple, theming, ambient mode, rotary input, `CurvedText`/`TimeText`, placeholders, hierarchical focus, accessibility.

